    "body": "The selected-source reader changes Copy and termination scores when query suffixes change, and the prior small development fit did not transfer. This implements a matched signed log-radius sharing comparison against the unrestricted radial grid using broader full-sequence Rust learning and sealed native checkpoints.\n\nBoth arms execute64updates and the predeclared native development CE criterion selects64: gridCE0.492382/31of64 complete; ratioCE0.951191/19of64. Both selected-only heldout panels complete0of32. Actual radial coefficients activate in both; retain all partial gains, losses and intermediate candidates. No default model or geometry-family verdict is adopted.\n\nValidation:54focused example tests and release build on exact committed a473523f; nativeCPU worker exit0/5511.224s; independent baseline/packing/optimizer/CE/action/prior-comparison review; complete393file SHA256 return verified. Documentation records the first pre-update resource refusal and210min complete charge. Claim-wording and diff checks pass. No GPU, Metal qualification, runners, energy or general-chat claim.\n\nThe roadmap advances to a fixed two-read pre-emission geometric refinement with learned role-separated query update control, after standalone native loader fidelity. Preserve source identity, joint alias/controller semantics and all retained candidates; depth remains an untested hypothesis.\n\nReferences #1552 and #1512.\n",
